import json,csv,hashlib
from pathlib import Path
b=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
q=list(csv.DictReader((b/'queue.csv').open()));ids=json.loads((b/'identity-audit.json').read_text());assert ids['downloads_sha256']==ids['population_recorded_downloads_sha256']
cl=json.loads((b/'lead-clocks.json').read_text());gg=json.loads((b/'lead-gaia-covariance.json').read_text());aa=json.loads((b/'lead-alias-covered-windows.json').read_text())
notes={
'1269035':('P','BYCATCH_GAIA_INCONSISTENT','Repeated narrow V eclipses at 20.48496 d, with broader shallower events between them. These are bounded eclipses rather than a smooth heartbeat. The selected Gaia period 29.0687 d fails the observed clock.','Gaia association fails; close blend and eccentric geometry remain incomplete; broader events were not used as independent same-kind timing epochs.','Resolve close companions and fit both eclipse kinds independently.'),
'22210159':('P','GAIA_ASSOCIATION_TENSION','Four deep narrow eclipses on flat baselines span S10 to S100. The eclipse clock 34.873695 d differs from Gaia34.843240 d by about4.5 formal Gaia period errors. Propagated Gaia conjunction offsets increase from0.829 to3.023 d, about3.9-4.4 local covariance sigma. Real repeated eclipses remain secure, but the Gaia geometry check fails at face value.','Gaia covariance is local linear and may understate orbit uncertainty; a wrong Gaia orbit or unresolved source remains possible; no independent eccentric solution is claimed.','Obtain new RVs or published RV reanalysis and two-kind eclipse geometry.'),
'34308477':('PLAUSIBLE','GAIA_ASSOCIATION_POSSIBLE','Two genuine eclipses occur at1442.69724 and2182.44887 BTJD. Their separation739.75163 d admits many integer-cycle aliases. The near-Gaia15-cycle value49.316776 d and its half24.658388 d survive existing coverage. The period is a candidate, not measured uniquely. Current-sector inventory includes S109; independent S109 extraction has gaps at the predicted event and provides no clean null for this value.','Only two same-kind occasions; many aliases remain. Gaia conjunction offsets2.406+-2.523 and4.176+-3.746 d are consistent but cannot select the clock alone.','Acquire a predicted eclipse at a time separating49.3168 and competing integer aliases.'),
'71295367':('P','SHORT_PERIOD_BYCATCH','Numerous sharp eclipses recur on a0.8710831 d deep-event clock across five sectors. Eighty-three covered deep-event windows contain deficits. Interleaved dips suggest a second eclipse kind; period halving and doubling require explicit odd/even geometry. Gaia20.2679 d cannot explain the train.','Orbital period versus alternating eclipse interval unresolved; no Gaia association or eccentricity claim; near blends remain bounded by pixel resolution.','Fit odd/even events and both kinds and obtain short-period RVs.'),
'92872537':('P','GAIA_ASSOCIATION_CONSISTENT','Deep flat-bottomed eclipses occur in S1,S68 and S95. The S95 eclipse at3893.70513 BTJD was absent from the original flagged-window list but is clear in raw full-sector flux and was fitted explicitly. Three occasions give32.816227 d. Timing-compatible null-free alternatives include65.63248 d; orbital doubling remains unresolved. Gaia32.80672+-0.04288 d and its propagated conjunctions agree.','Period32.81623 d is a favored recurrence; double65.63248 d remains possible if the sampled events alternate kinds. S95 strong baseline slope means local fitting is essential.','Observe a repeat separating the32.816 and65.632 d alternatives; fit secondary geometry.'),
'95324628':('P','SHORT_PERIOD_BYCATCH','Deep eclipses at2787.81866,3512.78381 and3523.14050 BTJD fit10.356645 d, including two same-kind events in S81. A shallower eclipse3525.83126 is at phase0.2598 after the primary, supporting noncircular geometry if it belongs to the same source. Gaia56.1241 d is incompatible.','No precise independent eccentric orbit; Gaia association fails. Exact-source external RV warning in arXiv2608.06453 says FEROS & RVs inconsistent with orbit; this weakens use of Gaia and is not prior EB evidence.','Fit both kinds and obtain/reanalyse RVs at10.35665 d; verify the RV literature row.'),
'98160330':('C','GAIA_ASSOCIATION_CONSISTENT','Five deep eclipses span S7,S33,S34,S87,S88. Consecutive-sector events directly recover30.22345 d; shallow eclipses recur at a different phase and are not counted as primary repeats. The period agrees with Gaia30.23494+-0.01150 d. Deep-event conjunction offsets are roughly1.6-2.6 local covariance sigma, with the earliest coarse-cadence epoch least consistent. Later primary and shallow-event phases are compatible with the eccentric Gaia orbit.','Period error is a conditional local covariance, not a calibrated total precision. TESS cannot exclude arbitrarily close companions; earliest30-minute timing has0.0127 d residual.','Higher cadence primary/secondary timing and RV characterization.'),
'98941880':('REFUTED','OFF_TARGET_CONTAMINATION','An eclipse train at4.3978035 d is real in QLP but the independent S90 deficit lies about3.7 pixels from the target at a bright southern source. A target-centered3x3 extraction has only about0.5 percent loss versus11 percent QLP. Difference image provides positive off-target evidence. S101 has five fully covered predicted cores with only2.0-2.6 ppt losses, showing strongly changing dilution/aperture coupling rather than stable target eclipses.','The contaminating source is not identified here. The measured4.3978 d clock describes the aperture signal, not the selected Gaia star.','Identify the southern eclipsing contaminant with Gaia-resolved or ground-based photometry.')}
rows=[]
for r in q:
 tic=r['tic'];sid=r['sample_id'];v,assoc,reason,lim,nxt=notes[tic];c=cl[tic];g=gg[tic];d=json.loads((b/tic/'lead-context.json').read_text());loc=json.loads((b/tic/'helper-localization.json').read_text());ev=json.loads((b/tic/'lead-timing.json').read_text());p=b/tic/'REPORT.md'
 lines=[f'# {sid}: TIC {tic}',f'Physical verdict: {v}. Full review completion: COMPLETE_BOUNDED. Association: {assoc}.',reason,'## Identity and provenance',f"Exact queue Gaia DR3 {r['gaia_dr3']}; nested population Gaia G={r['gaia_G']}. Raw hashes and FITS TIC/sector identities verified in ../identity-audit.json. Frozen source is fresh-band-next1000, not next400. Quality mask: finite positive SAP_FLUX, finite TIME, QUALITY=0. No discovery priority is assigned by this report.",'## Raw morphology and timing',f"Conditional recurrence period={c['period_d']:.9f} d; conditional formal period uncertainty={c['formal_period_error_d']:.9g} d. Assumed cycles={c['cycles']}; residuals(d)={c['residuals']}. These values depend on chosen kinds and integers. Duration median={c['duration_d']:.4f} d; fitted depth median={c['depth_ppt']:.2f} ppt. Local trapezoid covariance has cadence/2 and0.002d error floors in clock fit; failed/boundary fits are excluded.",'| Sector | Event BTJD | Depth ppt | Fit usable |','|---|---:|---:|---|']
 for e in ev:lines.append(f"| {e['sector']} | {e.get('center_btjd',0):.6f} | {e.get('depth_ppt',0):.2f} | {e.get('fit_usable',False)} |")
 lines+=['## Aliases and actual covered windows','Raw coverage audit in ../lead-alias-covered-windows.json requires quality-zero core coverage>=75%, no large core gap, and both sidebands. Flagged screen windows are not treated as nulls. The audit records per-window source hashes, depth and noise. Neighbor integer aliases were explicitly enumerated for sparse two-epoch cases; the timing_compatible field must also pass. No exhaustive period posterior is claimed.','| Trial | Period d | Covered | Clean low-depth windows |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
 for z in aa[tic][:6]:lines.append(f"| {z['label']} | {z['period_d']:.8f} | {z['covered']} | {len(z['nulls'])} |")
 lines+=['## Independent reduction and localization',f"Independent custom TESScut3x3 aperture extraction recovers event loss={loc['aperture_loss']:.5f}; deficit centroid offset={loc['centroid_offset_pixels']:.3f} TESS pixels. Local baseline-minus-event image and raw extraction are in helper-localization.png/json. This is a separate reduction of the SAME photons, not a new observing occasion. Capable neighbors and limitations are addressed in helper audit receipts.",'## Source-specific Gaia orbit',f"Gaia P={g['gaia_period_d']:.8f} +/-{g['gaia_period_error_d']:.8f} d; eccentricity={g['eccentricity']:.6f}; omega={g['omega_deg']:.4f} deg. ../lead-gaia-covariance.json derives edge-on conjunctions from this source's P,e,omega,Tp and full relevant Gaia covariance submatrix. Fixed-cycle local linear propagation is not a nonlinear posterior; high uncertainty and wrong Gaia orbits remain possible. Period equality alone is not an association test.",'## Limits and next check',lim,nxt,'## Catalogue status','Root-owned ../shared-catalogues contains controlled source-specific catalogue/literature receipts. Physical verdict is separate from novelty and publication eligibility. Successful bounded nonmatches do not prove exhaustive novelty.','## Evidence','lead-context.json; lead-series.json; lead-timing.json; lead-raw-context.png; helper-localization.json/png; ../identity-audit.json; ../lead-clocks.json; ../lead-gaia-covariance.json; ../lead-alias-covered-windows.json; ../helper audit.']
 p.write_text('\n\n'.join(lines)+'\n',encoding='utf8')
 rows.append(dict(sample_id=sid,tic=tic,gaia_dr3=r['gaia_dr3'],physical_verdict=v,full_review_completion='COMPLETE_BOUNDED',period_days=f"{c['period_d']:.9f}",period_interpretation='nonunique alias' if tic=='34308477' else 'conditional eclipse recurrence',association=assoc,limitations=lim,next_check=nxt,report=str(p)))
with (b/'RESULTS.csv').open('w',newline='',encoding='utf8') as f:w=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=rows[0]);w.writeheader();w.writerows(rows)
print('wrote',len(rows),'reports')
